ere are over 300 litter bins  throughout the district the bins offer a  convenient way for residents to dispose  of their waste when on the go the  majority of these are used correctly  however some litter bins are being  misused sacks of household or business  waste are being deposited in and around  her litter bins causing the bin to be  full and restricting the use for other  residents this is classed as fly-tipping  an investigation into the origins of the  waste will be carried out which could  lead to prosecution for details of how  to deal with excess household waste or  business waste phone recycling on 0170  2318 one double one or e-mail recycling  at Rochford gavotte UK calling all dog  owners are you being responsible it is  illegal to leave your dog's feces lying  around in a public area if a dog is in  your care for any length of time it is  your responsibility to clean up its mess  council officers regularly patrol the  district and irresponsible dog owners  could be issued with a 75-pound fixed  penalty notice for not picking up after  their dogs  dog fouling is unsightly unpleasant and  occur and can occasionally lead to  toxocariasis in humans which can cause  serious illness and even blindness  residents are also urged to dispose of  bagged feces correctly by placing them  into the nearest bin this can be a  general litter bin or dog waste bin bags  left on fences or trees will be treated  in the same way as not picking up the  feces to report a street seem problem  online w wh the govt UK / street scene  or you can email customer services at  Rochford gov UK or phone 0170 2318 111  recycle for essex what more can i do  make full use of your local recycling  centers can be rode on canvey island ss8  oqx Ferris Road south woodham ferrers  transferred cm3 5z a castle road  rayleigh ss6 7qf for more information on  opening times and what you can take  visit essex gov k 4 / recycling centers  or call 0845 6037 625 did you know that  you can take these 