r their bank card to a  career there are simple steps you can  take to avoid falling victim to this  type of crime do not give out your PIN  number do not give your bank card to a  courier if you suspect you have fallen  victim of fraud or someone has attempted  to defraud you please dial Essex Police  on 101 freecycle tagging with the warmer  weather on its way Railly and Rochford  neighborhood watch team will be  organising a free cycle tagging event  across the district throughout 2014  these events open to all residents of  Rochford district will provide bike  owners with an opportunity to have their  cycles fitted with security tags this  will make identification easier should  they be stolen dates and details of  these events will appear in a future  edition of Rochford district matters and  on the n HW website w WR r NW c om ze  com calling all schools if you would  like to arrange a date for n HW to carry  out cycle tagging in your schools please  contact n HW on 0 1 2 6 h 7 705 19 or  email n HW rayleigh @ gmail.com dance  don't chance bring on the prom the  clocks have sprung forward and summer is  well on its way young people across the  district will be thinking about  celebrating the transitions they are  facing with the biggest events being the  secondary school proms and balls each of  our secondary schools celebrate their  Year Elevens coming to the end of their  GCSE program with an event at the school  the students themselves sometimes want  to make the occasion extra special by  experimenting a little with things they  haven't done before it's a real  opportunity for getting dressed up in a  prom dress or suit and enjoying their  own adult party parents often want to  make it that extra special occasion  arranging memorable transport  and after parties the vast majority of  young people have a great time but there  are occasions where the experimenting  includes alcohol and drugs and if taken  they will reduce inhibitions and  reaction times they 